      "title": "HVAC SPECIALIST / BOILER OPERATOR (PART TIME)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-17\n\nLocation: Rochester Hills\n\nHVAC Specialist / Boiler Operator Facilities Department | Rochester Christian University | Rochester Hills, Michigan Position Summary Rochester Christian University is seeking a skilled and dependable  HVAC Specialist / Boiler Operator (Part Time)  to join the Facilities team. This position is responsible for the operation, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of campus HVAC, boiler, heating, cooling, ventilation, and domestic hot water systems. The position helps maintain a safe, comfortable, reliable, and energy-efficient campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Essential Responsibilities Operate, inspect, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair commercial HVAC systems, including air handlers, rooftop units, split systems, exhaust fans, VAV systems, pumps, motors, and related equipment. Operate, maintain, troubleshoot, and repair  commercial boilers and hot water systems . Monitor and adjust Building Automation System (BAS) controls to maintain proper building temperatures and improve energy efficiency. Perform scheduled preventative maintenance and equipment inspections. Diagnose electrical, mechanical, control, and HVAC system problems and complete necessary repairs. Maintain pumps, valves, piping, heat exchangers, thermostats, actuators, and related mechanical equipment. Respond to HVAC, heating, cooling, and mechanical service requests throughout campus. Assist with seasonal startup and shutdown of heating and cooling systems. Maintain accurate work orders, maintenance records, inspections, and equipment documentation. Coordinate with outside contractors and vendors as needed. Recommend equipment repairs, replacements, and energy-saving improvements. Maintain a safe, clean, and organized work environment and comply with applicable safety requirements. Participate in an on-call/emergency response as needed. Assist the Facilities team with other maintenance projects as needed. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED. Minimum  5 years of commercial HVAC experience . Minimum  3 years of commercial boiler operation and maintenance experience . Strong knowledge of HVAC, hydronic heating, electrical, mechanical, and control systems. Ability to troubleshoot and repair commercial mechanical equipment. Ability to read blueprints, wiring diagrams, and mechanical drawings. Valid Michigan driver's license and acceptable driving record. Ability to pass a background check. Preferred Qualifications HVAC certification or technical/trade school training. EPA Section 608 Universal Certification. Boiler Operator License or equivalent experience. Experience in higher education, institutional, commercial, or large-building facilities. Experience with Building Automation Systems (BAS) and/or computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS). Additional plumbing, electrical, or welding experience. Physical & Working Requirements Ability to lift up to 75 pounds, climb ladders, work from elevated platforms, and work in mechanical rooms, rooftops, crawl spaces, and other restricted areas. Position requires standing, bending, kneeling, stooping, and working indoors and outdoors in varying weather conditions. Must be available for occasional after-hours emergency response.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4ec54663-0058-4347-9828-d4720a7524f4&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201906917994_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "HEAD COACH - WOMEN'S FLAG FOOTBALL",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\n\nLocation: Rochester Hills\n\nJOB TITLE: Head Coach, Women’s Flag Football DEPARTMENT: Athletics REPORTS TO: Athletic Director/Vice President of Intercollegiate Athletics UNIVERSITY MISSION: Rochester University is a Christ-centered institution that empowers students to lead lives of personal and professional significance while serving God in a changing world. POSITION SUMMARY: Rochester Christian University invites applications for the founding Head Coach of Women's Flag Football. This is a unique opportunity for a mission-driven leader to build a new NAIA program from the ground up, establishing culture, systems, and competitive identity from its inaugural season forward. The Head Coach will be responsible for all aspects of the program, including recruiting, roster development, competitive scheduling, budget management, and the spiritual and personal formation of student-athletes, consistent with RCU's Christ-centered mission. EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE REQUIRED: Bachelor’s Degree in management, sports administration, or related field 1–3 years of athletic management experience, preferably at the college level Working knowledge of NAIA, conference, and collegiate compliance procedures preferred ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Lead the strategic launch and ongoing development of the Women's Flag Football program, including roster-building for the inaugural season. Recruit, evaluate, and retain student-athletes who fit RCU's academic standards, competitive goals, and Christian mission, in alignment with per-head enrollment and net-tuition-revenue goals.  Plan and conduct all practices, training sessions, and competitive game strategy in accordance with NAIA and WHAC rules and regulations. Develop and manage the program's operating budget, equipment, travel, and scheduling in coordination with the Athletics Business Office. Ensure full compliance with NAIA, WHAC, NCCAA, and RCU institutional rules, policies, and eligibility requirements. Mentor and disciple student-athletes, integrating faith and athletics consistent with RCU's Christ-centered mission and character-development priorities. Hire, supervise, and evaluate assistant coaches and program support staff as the program grows. Collaborate with Admissions, Student Financial Services, Academic Affairs, and Compliance to support student-athlete recruitment, enrollment, and academic success. Coordinate team travel, lodging, and game-day logistics in partnership with the athletics operations staff. Represent RCU professionally within the WHAC, NAIA, and NCCAA, and build relationships with regional high school and club flag football programs to grow the sport's pipeline. Engage in fundraising, community relations, and program promotion in partnership with the Advancement and Marketing offices. Uphold and model RCU's institutional mission, values, and Statement of Faith in all program operations. Perform other duties as assigned by the Vice President for Intercollegiate Athletics & Strategic Enrollment. SUPERVISORY DUTIES: Staff supervision Hire, onboard, and supervise assistant coach(es) as the program grows beyond year one Conduct performance evaluations of assistant coaches and any support staff (e.g., student managers, graduate assistants) Set practice plans, game-day assignments, and recruiting territories/responsibilities for assistants Approve staff time off, travel, and scheduling conflicts Student-athlete oversight (a quasi-supervisory function in college athletics) Oversee team captains and any student leadership structure Monitor academic progress and eligibility in coordination with Compliance and Academic Affairs Enforce team conduct standards, attendance policies, and RCU's Statement of Faith/community expectations Oversee locker room, travel, and off-campus conduct supervision during team activities Operational/budget supervision Approve and monitor spending against the program's per-head budget allocation (tying into RCU's existing tiered incentive model) Oversee equipment managers, film/video staff, or student workers assigned to the program Supervise game-day operations staff assigned to home flag football contests (in coordination with Athletics Operations) Compliance supervision Ensure assistant coaches and any recruiting-involved staff follow NAIA/WHAC recruiting rules Sign off on eligibility certifications and roster compliance. REQUIRED SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel regularly for practices, competitions, and recruiting. Ability to stand, walk, and move actively on a practice or competition field for extended periods. Occasional lifting of equipment (up to 25 lbs.).",
      "department": ""
